  "author": "Otohime <quiinthieu@gmail.com>\nOtohime <quiinthieu@gmail.com>\npm-258/t-1564: Run e2e files one at a time, give the footer walk and probe a throwaway database, and keep their checks apart from Kame\n\nSince 76141f1 \"E2E against next start\" failed on frame floors (the\ndesk's leaves, the Ryugu sea) because node --test ran the browser files\nside by side and they starved each other of frames. scripts/e2e.mjs now\npasses --test-concurrency=1; a later flag still wins.\nlib/e2e-runner.test.ts proves two files do not overlap, and that\n--test-concurrency=2 makes them overlap.\n\nscripts/e2e.mjs --serve-db <dir> holds its embedded Postgres, migrated,\nuntil SIGTERM. walk-end.sh and probe-end.sh use it when no database\nanswers and Docker is absent, and stop only their own process and\nwork dir. e2e.mjs now owns SIGINT/SIGTERM: embedded-postgres's\nasync-exit-hook used to exit first and leave the work dir (and the\nserver group) behind.\n\nThe Kame companion (dd21add) broke two checks. The probe's eyes budget\ncounted Kame's scroll edge frame from a late setup scroll event: it now\nwaits for scrolling to go quiet, and a new rAF negative control\noverlaps the two frames on purpose. ink-press's getByRole(\"status\")\nalso matched Kame's live region: it is now scoped to the press.\n\nThe footer waterline checks were repaired concurrently by 3351f78\n(pm-249/t-1568), so this commit does not touch them.\n\n",
